# New screen checklist

When adding or substantially editing a page under `src/ui/features/pages/`:

## 1. Route wiring

- Add lazy import in `src/App.jsx`: `const Foo = lazy(() => import("./ui/features/pages/FooPage.jsx"));`
- Add `<Route path="..." element={<Foo />} />` under the correct parent route.
- Add the path to `NAV_FULL` in `src/constants/userModes.js` if it is a navigable screen.

## 2. Page shell & i18n

- Wrap content in `PageShell` with `title={t("…")}` — **never hardcode English titles**.
- Add all new copy keys to `src/i18n/messages/en.js`, then run `npm run sync:i18n`.

## 3. Empty states

- List screens (bills, spends, lending, goals) must render `EmptyState` or `GuidedEmptyState`.
- Register guided empty states in `src/guidance/registry/emptyStates.js` with a stable key.
- Use `GuidedEmptyState` with `guidanceKey="…"` for primary product lists.

## 4. Mobile / device resize

- Use `ct-*` layout classes — no fixed pixel widths on page containers.
- Prefer `100dvh` / `min-height: 100dvh` over `100vh` for full-height layouts.
- Bottom sheets and modals must respect `env(safe-area-inset-*)` (see `components.css`).
- Test mentally at 320px width — no horizontal scroll on the main column.

## 5. Accessibility

- Icon-only buttons and FABs need `aria-label={t("…")}`.
- Modals/sheets use `role="dialog"` + `aria-modal="true"` (see `Modal.jsx`).

## 6. Verify

```bash
npm run audit          # full gate including governance
npm run audit:ui-depth # route/nav wiring
```
